1
00:01:02,537 --> 00:01:05,515
You ready for the next problem?

2
00:01:05,515 --> 00:01:06,515
You know what?

3
00:01:06,515 --> 00:01:08,493
I can't look at another number.

4
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:10,493
How about a lemonade break?

5
00:01:10,493 --> 00:01:14,449
Sure.

6
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:15,949
Oh, by the way,

7
00:01:15,949 --> 00:01:19,927
when is your plane reservation for your flight to Athens?

8
00:01:19,927 --> 00:01:20,780
Sunday. Why?

9
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:25,783
Would you be able to come over Saturday night?

10
00:01:25,783 --> 00:01:26,361
Yes.

11
00:01:26,361 --> 00:01:29,339
I should be finished packing by then.

12
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:32,317
My folks are giving me a little graduation party.

13
00:01:32,317 --> 00:01:33,317
Terrific!

14
00:01:33,317 --> 00:01:35,295
I'll pick you up.

15
00:01:35,295 --> 00:01:36,935
That isn't necessary.

16
00:01:36,935 --> 00:01:38,843
My dad's letting me borrow the car.

17
00:01:38,843 --> 00:01:42,563
Oh, well, that would be very nice.

18
00:01:42,563 --> 00:01:43,638
About eight o'clock?

19
00:01:43,638 --> 00:01:45,201
Eight o'clock is fine.

20
00:01:45,201 --> 00:01:46,582
Great! It's a date.

21
00:01:46,582 --> 00:01:50,185
Who's going to be there?

22
00:01:50,185 --> 00:01:53,163
Just my friend Mike and a few kids from school.

23
00:01:53,163 --> 00:01:55,877
I'm going to miss all of you.

24
00:01:55,877 --> 00:01:58,765
You've been like a second family to me.

25
00:01:58,765 --> 00:02:00,990
We're going to miss you.

26
00:02:00,990 --> 00:02:04,576
Maybe you could come to visit me in Greece?

27
00:02:04,576 --> 00:02:06,061
I'm counting on it.

28
00:02:06,061 --> 00:02:06,554
Wonderful!

29
00:02:06,554 --> 00:02:11,519
Are you excited about graduating from high school?

30
00:02:11,519 --> 00:02:14,008
Sure ... and a little scared.

31
00:02:14,008 --> 00:02:14,808
Scared? Why?

32
00:02:14,808 --> 00:02:18,186
Aren't you a little scared?

33
00:02:18,186 --> 00:02:22,824
I was when I first came to the United States.

34
00:02:22,824 --> 00:02:23,862
I'd never been away from home,

35
00:02:23,862 --> 00:02:26,670
and I didn't know what it would be like.

36
00:02:26,670 --> 00:02:32,543
But then I found out that people are the same everywhere

37
00:02:32,543 --> 00:02:34,876
once you get to know them.

38
00:02:34,876 --> 00:02:36,374
I'm glad I got to know you.

39
00:02:36,374 --> 00:02:37,674
Thank you.

40
00:02:37,674 --> 00:02:40,810
I'm glad I got to know you--and your family.

41
00:02:40,810 --> 00:02:44,388
Wouldn't it be nice if we could skip the examinations

42
00:02:44,388 --> 00:02:46,488
and get right to the graduation party?

43
00:02:46,488 --> 00:02:49,070
It would be very nice.

44
00:02:49,070 --> 00:02:51,744
But that isn't the way it works.

45
00:02:51,744 --> 00:02:58,678
So ... back to work.

46
00:02:58,678 --> 00:02:59,442
Good night, Robbie.

47
00:02:59,442 --> 00:03:00,460
Good night, Mrs. Stewart.

48
00:03:00,460 --> 00:03:01,900
Thank you for dinner.

49
00:03:01,900 --> 00:03:02,634
Good night, Alexandra.

50
00:03:02,634 --> 00:03:03,856
Will you be all right?

51
00:03:03,856 --> 00:03:07,612
Yes. The Molinas are waiting for me.

52
00:03:07,612 --> 00:03:08,677
Good night, Alexandra.

53
00:03:08,677 --> 00:03:16,545
I'll pick you up on Saturday night, OK?

54
00:03:16,545 --> 00:03:22,501
Yes.

55
00:03:22,501 --> 00:03:30,457
I have to run.

56
00:03:30,457 --> 00:03:33,115
Good night, Robbie.

57
00:03:33,115 --> 00:03:37,391
She's really a good friend, isn't she?

58
00:03:37,391 --> 00:03:43,347
Yeah.

59
00:03:43,347 --> 00:03:50,803
You are going to miss her.

60
00:03:50,803 --> 00:04:14,127
Am I going to miss her?

61
00:04:14,127 --> 00:04:15,127
That's what I said!

62
00:04:15,127 --> 00:04:25,038
You are going to miss her!

63
00:04:25,038 --> 00:04:37,458
I'm going to miss her,

64
00:04:37,458 --> 00:04:43,813
and my math teacher's going to miss her.

65
00:04:43,813 --> 00:05:25,206
Well, you can write to her.

66
00:05:25,206 --> 00:05:34,103
It's not the same.

67
00:05:34,103 --> 00:05:36,509
How does that look, Rob?

68
00:05:36,509 --> 00:05:39,860
Great! Pass me the hammer.

69
00:05:39,860 --> 00:05:41,722
You got it!

70
00:05:41,722 --> 00:05:49,171
You're sure Alexandra's going to be surprised?

71
00:05:49,171 --> 00:05:49,546
Absolutely.

72
00:05:49,546 --> 00:06:00,973
She has no idea that the party is in her honor.

73
00:06:00,973 --> 00:06:03,858
Millie, did you bring the tapes for dancing? Millie

74
00:06:03,858 --> 00:06:04,951
They're in my bag.

75
00:06:04,951 --> 00:06:06,577
What did you bring?

76
00:06:06,577 --> 00:06:07,729
Some rock 'n' roll.

77
00:06:07,729 --> 00:06:09,267
Perfect! Alexandra will love it!

78
00:06:09,267 --> 00:06:21,179
I can't wait to see her face when she walks in here tonight.

79
00:06:21,179 --> 00:06:24,815
What about the cake?

80
00:06:24,815 --> 00:06:26,788
My mom's decorating it right now.

81
00:06:26,788 --> 00:06:35,285
Robbie, there's a phone call for you. Robbie

82
00:06:35,285 --> 00:06:36,569
It's Alexandra.

83
00:06:36,569 --> 00:06:39,047
She sounds upset.

84
00:06:39,047 --> 00:06:39,544
OK.

85
00:06:39,544 --> 00:06:42,025
I'll take it in there.

86
00:06:42,025 --> 00:06:43,025
Hi, Alexandra.

87
00:06:43,025 --> 00:06:45,378
What? You what?

88
00:06:45,378 --> 00:06:48,378
Oh no!
